tics is an automatic machine that performs various tasks that were previously done \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 by humans. \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb0\sl-276\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li1799\sb11\sl-276\slmult0\tx3693 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Question No: 38 \tab \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 ( Marks: 5 ) \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb4\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 How many ways are there to call a function in a program? Explain with example. \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb264\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 Two Ways of Calling Functions: \par\pard\qj \li1799\sb0\sl-280\slmult0 \par\pard\qj\li1799\ri2052\sb1\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 Functions do not run automatically. When the page loads, each function waits quietly \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 until it is told to run. \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb264\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 1. A function calls appearing as a complete statement: \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb0\sl-276\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li1799\sb8\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 function popUp( message ) \{ \par\pard\ql \li1799\ri3980\sb1\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 window.alert( message ) ; \line \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 \} \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb1\sl-255\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 popUp( \u8220?Warning!\u8221? ) ; \par\pard\qj \li1799\sb0\sl-280\slmult0 \par\pard\qj\li1799\ri2002\sb5\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 2. A function calls appearing as part of a statement. Definitions of such functions \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 include a \u8216?return\u8217? statement: \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb264\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 function add( a, b ) \{ \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb4\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 c = a + b ; \par\pard\ql \li1799\ri4786\sb1\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 return c ; \line \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 \} \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb4\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 sum = add( 2, 4 ) ; \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb1\sl-256\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 document.write( sum ) ; \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb0\sl-276\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li1799\sb12\sl-276\slmult0\tx3693 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Question No: 39 \tab \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 ( Marks: 5 ) \par\pard\ql \li3824\sb0\sl-287\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li3824\sb8\sl-287\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex108 \ul0\nosupersub\cf6\f7\fs25 Note\ul0\nosupersub\cf7\f8\fs25 : Solve these papers by yourself \par\pard\ql \li2702\sb74\sl-287\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex106 This VU Group is not responsible for any solved content \par\pard\sect\sectd\fs24\paperw12240\paperh15840{\shp
