. \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb4\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 The web page will ask the user to enter five values to be added. \par\pard\qj \li1799\ri1749\sb1\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 After taking input it will calculate the sum and mean of those values by calling sum \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 and mean functions. \par\pard\li1799\sb0\sl-276\slmult0\par\pard\li1799\sb0\sl-276\slmult0\par\pard\li1799\sb2\sl-276\slmult0\fi0\tx3693 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 Question No: 41\tab \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 ( Marks: 10 )\par\pard\li1799\sb0\sl-274\slmult0\fi0 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 Define the following terms.\par\pard\li1799\sb0\sl-276\slmult0\par\pard\li1799\sb3\sl-276\slmult0\fi0 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Object\par\pard\li1799\sb0\sl-274\slmult0\fi0\tx6514\tx9179 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 Object  is  a  named  collection  of  properties\tab \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 (data,  state)  &  methods\tab \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 (instructions,\par\pard\li1799\sb1\sl-276\slmult0\fi0 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 behavior).\par\pard\ql \li1799\sb276\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Event Handler \par\pard\qj \li1799\ri1609\sb0\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 An event handler is a command which calls a function when an event happens, such as \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 the user clicking a button. \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb265\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Local Variable \par\pard\qj \li1799\ri1610\sb18\sl-260\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 Declaring variables (using the var keyword) within a function makes them local. They are \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 available only within the function and hold no meaning outside of it. \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb0\sl-276\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li1799\sb11\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Scope of Variable \par\pard\qj \li1799\ri1611\sb1\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 Defining the space in which a variable is effective is known as defining the scope of a \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 variable. A variable can be either local or global in scope. \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb264\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Array \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb4\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 Array is an indexed list of elements. \par\pard\ql \li1799\ri3753\sb1\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Question No: 27 ( Marks: 1 ) \line \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 What BIOS stands for? \par\pard\ql \li1859\sb1\sl-255\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 BIOS stand for Basic input/output system. \par\pard\ql \li3824\sb0\sl-287\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li3824\sb32\sl-287\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex108 \ul0\nosupersub\cf6\f7\fs25 Note\ul0\nosupersub\cf7\f8\fs25 : Solve these papers by yourself \par\pard\ql \li2702\sb74\sl-287\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex106 This VU Group is not responsible for any solved content \par\pard\sect\sectd\fs24\paperw12240\paperh15840{\shp
