ndtw-5\charscalex100 ( Marks: 3 ) \par\pard\ql \li1859\sb1\sl-256\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 How can you define a consistent web design? Why is it needed? \par\pard\qj \li1799\ri1610\sb5\sl-280\slmult0\fi59 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 A consistent good designed website is generated for general public that allows users to \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 attain what they want as quickly as possible without spending much effort.\ul0\nosupersub\cf11\f12\fs24  \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 A consistent \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 good design is needed to assists the user in recovering from errors. \par\pard\ql \li1859\sb4\sl-276\slmult0\tx3753 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Question No: 36 \tab \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 ( Marks: 3 ) \par\pard\qj \li1859\ri2767\sb0\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 How can we include images in a web page using HTML and Java script? \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 Image in HTML \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb1\sl-257\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 <IMG src=URL, alt=text height=pixels width=pixels align="bottom|middle|top"> \par\pard\ql \li1859\sb8\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Image in Javascript \par\pard\qj \li1799\ri1864\sb18\sl-260\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 Images in JavaScript can be manipulated in many ways using the built-in object Image. \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 Additional properties to HTML are hspace, vspace & lowsrc. \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb7\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 Example: It can be used by many handlers like, onAbort, onLoad & onError \par\pard\li1799\sb14\sl-276\slmult0\fi0\tx3693 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Question No: 37\tab \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 ( Marks: 3 )\par\pard\li1799\sb0\sl-274\slmult0\fi59 \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 The event handler attribute consists of three parts. Write about each of them\ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 .\par\pard\li1799\sb1\sl-276\slmult0\fi0\tx2339 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 1.\tab \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 The identifier of the event handler.\par\pard\li1799\sb0\sl-276\slmult0\fi0\tx2339 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 2.\tab \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 The equal sign.\par\pard\li1799\sb0\sl-276\slmult0\fi0\tx2339 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 3.\tab \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 A string consisting of JavaScript statements enclosed in double or single quotes.\par\pard\li1799\sb2\sl-276\slmult0\fi0\tx3693 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Question No: 38\tab \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 (Marks: 5 )\par\pard\qj \li1799\ri2068\sb0\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 What is a packet in the network environment? What kind of information does it \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 contain? \par\pard\qj \li1799\ri1609\sb252\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 A packet is the smallest unit of data transmitted over a computer network. It\u8217?s a message \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex107 to be transferred over the network is broken up into small packets by the sending \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 computer. \par\pard\ql \li1799\ri3247\sb261\sl-280\slmult0\fi59 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 Each packet contains the following info: \line \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 -Sender's address \par\pard\ql \li1799\ri4216\sb1\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 -Destination address \line \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 -Data \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb1\sl-255\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 -Error-recovery info. \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb8\sl-276\slmult0\tx3693 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Question No: 39 \tab \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 ( Marks: 5 ) \par\pard\ql \li3824\sb0\sl-287\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li3824\sb28\sl-287\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex108 \ul0\nosupersub\cf6\f7\fs25 Note\ul0\nosupersub\cf7\f8\fs25