s to maintain a list of people (contacts) \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 that we interact with regularly. We can send instant messages to any of the contacts in \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 our list as long as that contact is online. \par\pard\ql \li1859\sb1\sl-255\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 Following steps are involved in IM working: \par\pard\li2159\sb20\sl-276\slmult0\fi0\tx2699 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 1.\tab \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 User commences the IM client.\par\pard\li2159\sb0\sl-276\slmult0\fi0\tx2699 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 2.\tab \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 IM client finds the IM server & logs in.\par\pard\li2159\sb0\sl-276\slmult0\fi0\tx2699 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 3.\tab \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 It launches communication info (IP address, etc) to the IM server.\par\pard\li2159\sb0\sl-276\slmult0\fi0\tx2699 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 4.\tab \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex100 IM server finds user\u8217?s contacts & sends him/her the communication info.\par\pard\li2159\sb0\sl-276\slmult0\fi0\tx2768 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 5.\tab \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex100 IM server also notifies the contacts that the user is online; sends his/her\par\pard\li2159\sb0\sl-276\slmult0\fi0 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 communication info to them.\par\pard\li2159\sb0\sl-276\slmult0\fi0\tx2699 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 6.\tab \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex100 The user\u8217?s & the contact\u8217?s IM clients are ready to communicate directly (P2P).\par\pard\li2159\sb0\sl-276\slmult0\fi0\tx2716 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 7.\tab \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex100 As new contact has come online, IM server informs them about the user being\par\pard\li2159\sb0\sl-276\slmult0\fi0 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 online & vice versa.\par\pard\li2159\sb0\sl-276\slmult0\fi0\tx2699 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 8.\tab \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 Multiple, real-time chat are possible.\par\pard\li2159\sb0\sl-276\slmult0\fi0\tx2701 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 9.\tab \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 When the user logs-off, his/her IM client informs the IM server.\par\pard\qj \li2159\ri1610\sb0\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 10.   IM server wipes away the temporary file and informs the user\u8217?s contact\u8217?s about \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 his/her \u8216?offline\u8217? status. \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb1\sl-266\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Question No: 5 ( Marks: 10 ) \par\pard\qj \li1799\ri1675\sb0\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 What kind of operations takes place inside Microprocessors Building Blocks? Enlist \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 them with brief description. \par\pard\qj \li1799\sb0\sl-270\slmult0 \par\pard\qj\li1799\sb0\sl-270\slmult0 \par\pard\qj\li1799\ri1609\sb12\sl-270\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 Bus Interface Unit: \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 The bus interface unit is the part of the processor that interfaces with \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex100 the rest of the PC. Its name comes from the fact that it deals with moving information \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 over the processor data bus. \par\pard\qj \li1799\sb0\sl-270\slmult0 \par\pard\qj\li1799\ri1610\sb21\sl-270\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-1\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Instruction Decoder: \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 The \ul0\nosupersub\cf12\f13\fs24 instruction decoder \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 of a processor is a combinatorial circuit \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex103 sometimes in the form of a read-only memory, sometimes in the form of an ordinary \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 combinatorial circuit. \par\pard\ql \li3824\sb0\sl-287\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li3824\sb29\sl-287\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex108 \ul0\nosupersub\cf6\f7\fs25 Note\ul0\nosupersub\cf7\f8\fs25 : Solve these papers by yourself \par\pard\ql \li2702\sb74\sl-287\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex106 This VU Group is not responsible for any solved content \par\pard\sect\sectd\fs24\paperw1224