p0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 access to commonly used values. \par\pard\qj \li1799\ri1610\sb261\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex109 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Control Unit: \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 A control unit is the part of a CPU or other device that directs its \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 operation. The outputs of the unit control the activity of the rest of the device. \par\pard\qj \li1799\sb0\sl-280\slmult0 \par\pard\qj\li1799\ri1610\sb1\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Instruction Set:  \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 This is the set of machine instructions that a microprocessor recognizes \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 and can execute. It is the only language microprocessor knows. \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb264\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Question No: 7 ( Marks: 8 ) \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb4\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 a) Differentiate between SMTP and POP3 server. (3 marks) \par\pard\qj \li1799\sb0\sl-275\slmult0 \par\pard\qj\li1799\ri1610\sb10\sl-275\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex103 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 SMTP (Simple Mail Transfer Protocol) is a protocol used to send and receive eMail \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex100 messages over a TCP/IP network. Whereas POP3 (Post Office Protocol) is a protocol \up0 \expndtw-2\charscalex100 used for receiving eMail messages. A POP3 server maintains text files (one file per user \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex103 accounts) containing all messages received by a user. eMail client interacts with the \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 POP3 server for discovering and downloading new eMail messages. \par\pard\qj \li1799\sb0\sl-280\slmult0 \par\pard\qj\li1799\ri2229\sb261\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 b) How can you justify that a DBMS is better to use than Flat-file database? (5 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 marks) \par\pard\qj \li1799\sb0\sl-270\slmult0 \par\pard\qj\li1799\ri1609\sb19\sl-270\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex103 \ul0\nosupersub\cf5\f6\fs24 A DBMS takes care of the storage, retrieval, and management of large data sets on a \line \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex100 Database. It provides SW tools needed to organize & manipulate that data in a flexible \line \up0 \expndtw-3\charscalex100 manner. \par\pard\qj \li1799\sb0\sl-280\slmult0 \par\pard\qj\li1799\ri1610\sb2\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex103 Whereas in Flat-file database the text file format makes it hard to search for specific \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 information or to create reports that include only certain fields from each record. \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb264\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 \ul0\nosupersub\cf9\f10\fs24 Question No: 8 ( Marks: 8 ) \par\pard\qj \li1799\ri1949\sb1\sl-280\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-4\charscalex100 What will be the output of this programme? Write comments where you find \u8220?//\u8221? \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 symbol in the following code. \par\pard\ql \li1799\sb264\sl-276\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw-5\charscalex100 <html> \par\pard\ql \li3824\sb0\sl-287\slmult0 \par\pard\ql\li3824\sb28\sl-287\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex108 \ul0\nosupersub\cf6\f7\fs25 Note\ul0\nosupersub\cf7\f8\fs25 : Solve these papers by yourself \par\pard\ql \li2702\sb74\sl-287\slmult0 \up0 \expndtw0\charscalex106 This VU Group is not responsible for any solved content \par\pard\sect\sectd\fs24\paperw12240\paperh15840{\shp
